,title,link,text,language,family
0,Palaung language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaung_language,"The Palaung people are divided into Palé (Ruching), Rumai, and Shwe, and each of whom have their own language. The Riang languages are reported to be unintelligible or only understood with great difficulty by native speakers of the other Palaung languages.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
1,Palaung | PLP,https://www.phoenixlanguageproject.org/palaung,"Paulang has three varieties: Ruching, Rumai, and Shwe. Although they are mutually intelligible (they can understand each other), the three varieties vary significantly in grammar and lexicon.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
2,Ruching Palaung / Pale Palaung - Max Planck Society,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Palaung-Ruching.htm,"Other comments: Ruching Palaung or Pale Palaung or De'ang or Da'ang is spoken by approximately 273,000 speakers in Yunnan province, China a well as Mandalay region and Taunggyi district in Shan state, Myanmar and northern Thailand. Ruching Palaung has a decimal system.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
3,Palaung language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Palaung_language/,"Palaung or Ta'ang, also known as De'ang (;), is an Austroasiatic dialect cluster spoken by over half a million people in Burma (Shan State) and neighboring countries.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
4,Palaungic languages — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Palaungic_languages,"The Eastern branch consists of the Palaung-Riang and Danau subgroups, while the Western branch includes the Waic (encompassing Wa and Lamet) and Angkuic (including Mok) subgroups.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
5,AUSTROASIATIC: VIETNAMESE & PALAUNG - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z6cr0eJbIls,"Mar 7, 2025 · Palaung is a tonal language with several dialects, and while it is primarily an oral language, some efforts have been made to develop writing systems using Burmese or Latin scripts.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
6,"Palaung alphabet, prounciation and language - Omniglot",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/palaung.htm,"There are three varieties of Palaung: Ruching, Rumai and Shwe, which are classified as separate languages by some people. Ruching has about 273,000 speakers, and is also known as Da'ang, Di-Ang, Ngwe Palaung, Palay or Silver Palaung.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
7,Austro-Asiatic | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/231/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..APr-rm8w7NaDHs8J5o9dkC9NNQhJOHRHauOk2RJyE2Q,"Austro-Asiatic. Subgroup of 167 languages. Collapse All.Palaung, Ruching pce, a language of Myanmar.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
8,Austro-Asiatic Language Family - Structure & Dialects - MustGo,https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/austro-asiatic-language-family/,"The Austro-Asiatic language family consists of 169 languages spoken in Southeast Asia, in countries located between China and Indonesia. A few are spoken to the west of this area in the Nicobar Islands and in India. The austro– part of the name comes from the Latin word for ‘south.’","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
9,Ruching Palaung - pce (Austro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/pce/,"Bible Resources for Ruching Palaung: 2012 Edition – Ruching Palaung (pce). Provided by Faith Comes by Hearing. People Groups who primarily speak Ruching Palaung. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.","Palaung, Ruching",Austro-Asiatic
